questions.question:
The browser reads the Hint Service stream with this code. It passed every manual test on localhost:

const reader = res.body.pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream()).getReader();
for (;;) {
  const { value, done } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  if (value.startsWith("data: [DONE]")) break;
  const frame = JSON.parse(value.slice(6));   // "data: " is 6 characters
  hintBox.textContent += frame.delta;
}

Production error log, behind the CDN, same day:

SyntaxError: Unterminated string in JSON at position 26
  value = 'data: {"delta":"Check what sumSc'   (length 32)
SyntaxError: Unexpected token 'e', "eturns"}\n\n"... is not valid JSON
  value = 'ores returns"}\n\ndata: {"delta":" for []"}\n\n'   (length 43)

Statement: "These errors show that the model produced invalid JSON in its deltas, so the fix is a stricter prompt that tells the model to always close its strings."

